21
00:01:09,433 --> 00:01:13,211
The handoffs are the point. An event is the question,

22
00:01:13,211 --> 00:01:16,990
not the answer. Evidence gives it a traceable basis. Exposure

23
00:01:16,990 --> 00:01:20,013
asks which issuers and instruments may be affected.

24
00:01:20,013 --> 00:01:23,563
A scenario makes assumptions visible: what could happen, what could

25
00:01:23,563 --> 00:01:27,114
go the other way, and which new fact would change

26
00:01:27,114 --> 00:01:30,664
the view. On the market map, token labels, provider timestamps,

27
00:01:30,664 --> 00:01:34,215
and session context distinguish a public quote from a complete

28
00:01:34,215 --> 00:01:37,766
investment picture. Tokenized instruments can differ in hours, liquidity, and

29
00:01:37,766 --> 00:01:41,316
issuer terms. A price is one observation; it does not

30
00:01:41,316 --> 00:01:44,867
prove that an asset can trade at that level or

31
00:01:44,867 --> 00:01:46,997
that a strategy can execute there.

32
00:01:46,997 --> 00:01:50,845
For a market idea, Strategy Lab turns a rule into

33
00:01:50,845 --> 00:01:54,692
a reproducible historical replay. Choose an instrument, interval, and deterministic

34
00:01:54,692 --> 00:01:58,540
strategy; review the costs, data window, holdout, and trade record.

35
00:01:58,540 --> 00:02:02,387
The published validation is candid: its tested baseline underperformed buy

36
00:02:02,387 --> 00:02:06,235
and hold across five markets in that snapshot. It is

37
00:02:06,235 --> 00:02:09,697
an experiment to inspect, not a claim of alpha.

38
00:02:09,697 --> 00:02:13,562
The hackathon’s Alpha Factory bar asks for at least sixty

39
00:02:13,562 --> 00:02:17,427
calendar days with thirty out of sample, so that qualification

40
00:02:17,427 --> 00:02:21,291
matters. Strategy Lab replays deterministic rules over completed public candles,

41
00:02:21,291 --> 00:02:25,156
with a chronological holdout and explicit fee and slippage assumptions.

42
00:02:25,156 --> 00:02:29,020
Tidelight records the window and outputs so a result can

43
00:02:29,020 --> 00:02:32,885
be examined and repeated. A replay helps test a rule;

44
00:02:32,885 --> 00:02:35,977
one short sample does not prove durable performance.

45
00:02:35,977 --> 00:02:39,776
Nightwatch carries the same discipline into paper mode. It reviews

46
00:02:39,776 --> 00:02:43,576
completed Bitget candles, records why it proposes or declines an

47
00:02:43,576 --> 00:02:47,376
action, and applies explicit account and loss limits before a

48
00:02:47,376 --> 00:02:51,175
simulated fill. Its ledger is private to a signed-in workspace.

49
00:02:51,175 --> 00:02:54,975
This public view is logged out; no private decisions or

50
00:02:54,975 --> 00:02:56,875
fills are being shown here.

51
00:02:56,875 --> 00:03:00,912
No live exchange orders are sent. Nightwatch reviews completed candles

52
00:03:00,912 --> 00:03:04,950
and paper-account context, then records rationale, confidence, risks, and invalidation.

53
00:03:04,950 --> 00:03:08,987
A hard risk rule can reject a proposal, and a

54
00:03:08,987 --> 00:03:13,025
hold is a valid outcome. Fees and slippage are estimated;

55
00:03:13,025 --> 00:03:15,448
simulated fills are not exchange fills.

56
00:03:15,448 --> 00:03:19,303
A signed-in workspace is needed to show its private ledger.

57
00:03:19,303 --> 00:03:23,158
The trading pages expose distinct review paths, including simulated workflows.

58
00:03:23,158 --> 00:03:27,013
This walkthrough does not connect an exchange account, submit a

59
00:03:27,013 --> 00:03:30,868
live order, or suggest that a paper result is ready

60
00:03:30,868 --> 00:03:34,723
for execution. Human judgment remains at the center: inspect the

61
00:03:34,723 --> 00:03:38,578
source, understand the market context, test the assumption, and decide

62
00:03:38,578 --> 00:03:40,891
whether the question deserves another look.

63
00:03:40,891 --> 00:03:43,817
Event. Evidence. Exposure. Scenario.

64
00:03:43,817 --> 00:03:47,061
Decision. Tidelight brings the pieces into one calmer market desk—so

65
00:03:47,061 --> 00:03:50,305
